    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1259">

                <pb facs="1246" n="1236" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3393/3–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-14T18:00:00+08:00">March 14, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 14—6:33 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>874. Admiral Crawford<anchor n="53" xml:id="d1259-f1"/> informs me Marine
                    Battalion now here will be replaced March 18 by another Tsingtao battalion.
                    Since this will result in no net increase number Marines here and is only to
                    prevent those now here from going stale, I see no objection. Navy prefers no
                    publicity since this is another move reduce strength at Tsingtao, so will say
                    nothing here unless hand forced or Department instructs.<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d1259-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Nanking 519.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1259-f1" n="53" xml:id="d1259-f1-content">
                <p>Rear Adm. George C. Crawford, Commander of Amphibious Group No. 3 and Task Force
                    78 at Shanghai.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1259-f2" n="54" xml:id="d1259-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 911, March 17, 3 p. m., the Consul General at Shanghai reported:
                    “Navy reconsidered earlier views re publicity on Shanghai relief 9th Marines by
                    3rd Marines and issued public statement this morning without advising Consulate
                    General.” (811.3393/3–1749)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
